<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">ExxonMobil</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1999">1999</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Exxon Mobil Corporation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">ExxonMobil is an American oil and gas company formed in 1999 by the merger of Exxon and Mobil, both descended from John D. Rockefeller's Standard Oil. One of the world's largest companies, it discovered the large Liza oil field off Guyana in 2015 and began production there in 2019, transforming Guyana's economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/exxonmobil.jpg" alt="ExxonMobil" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lanzao0o1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cube_xom_mine.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
